{
  "topic": "The science of tsunamis",
  "language": "en",
  "format": "long",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "TSUNAMIS: the Science of the Wave That Crosses Oceans 🌊",
  "hook": "How can a single wave cross an entire ocean and reach the other side of the world?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_hook",
      "narration": "How can a single wave cross an entire ocean and reach the other side of the world?",
      "on_screen_text": "A wave that crosses oceans",
      "highlight_words": [
        "oceans"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_small",
      "narration": "And the strangest part: out at sea you can barely notice it. A ship could ride over it without feeling a thing.",
      "on_screen_text": "Barely noticeable at sea",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Barely"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_plates",
      "narration": "I'm Leo, and today I'll explain the real science of tsunamis, and most importantly, how to stay safe.",
      "on_screen_text": "The real science",
      "highlight_words": [
        "real"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_plates",
      "narration": "Scientists can't predict the exact day of an earthquake, but they can detect a tsunami within minutes.",
      "on_screen_text": "Detected in minutes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "minutes"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_push",
      "narration": "Most tsunamis start under the sea, where one plate of the crust dives beneath another.",
      "on_screen_text": "Colliding plates",
      "highlight_words": [
        "plates"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "How it starts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_quake",
      "narration": "For years the plates get stuck. When they finally slip, the seafloor jumps all at once: that's a great earthquake.",
      "on_screen_text": "The seafloor jumps",
      "highlight_words": [
        "jumps"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_quake",
      "narration": "The biggest tsunamis come from very large earthquakes, magnitude eight or more, when the seafloor moves vertically.",
      "on_screen_text": "Huge earthquakes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Huge"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_lift",
      "narration": "That jump pushes up the entire column of water, from the bottom to the surface, over a huge area.",
      "on_screen_text": "All the water rises",
      "highlight_words": [
        "water"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_spread",
      "narration": "Then the water drops back down, and that energy spreads out in waves moving in every direction.",
      "on_screen_text": "Waves in every direction",
      "highlight_words": [
        "direction"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_spread",
      "narration": "Landslides and volcanoes can trigger them too, but earthquakes are the most common cause.",
      "on_screen_text": "The most common cause",
      "highlight_words": [
        "common"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_speed",
      "narration": "In deep water, a tsunami travels at more than eight hundred kilometers per hour, as fast as a jet plane.",
      "on_screen_text": "As fast as a jet",
      "highlight_words": [
        "jet"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Fast as a jet"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_small",
      "narration": "But out there it's a meter tall or less. What makes it dangerous isn't its height but its length: hundreds of kilometers of moving water.",
      "on_screen_text": "Low but very long",
      "highlight_words": [
        "long"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_pacific",
      "narration": "In nineteen sixty, a tsunami born in Chile crossed the whole Pacific and reached Japan about twenty-two hours later.",
      "on_screen_text": "Chile → Japan: 22 hours",
      "highlight_words": [
        "22"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_grow",
      "narration": "As it nears the coast, the seafloor gets shallow. The front slows down and the back catches up.",
      "on_screen_text": "It slows and piles up",
      "highlight_words": [
        "piles"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Reaching the coast"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_grow",
      "narration": "All that water piles up and the wave grows, sometimes many meters tall.",
      "on_screen_text": "The wave grows",
      "highlight_words": [
        "grows"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_hook",
      "narration": "And it's not just one wave: several usually arrive over hours, and the first isn't always the biggest.",
      "on_screen_text": "Several waves arrive",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Several"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_retreat",
      "narration": "Sometimes, before it arrives, the sea suddenly pulls back and leaves the beach exposed. That's a warning sign.",
      "on_screen_text": "The sea pulls back",
      "highlight_words": [
        "pulls"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_pacific",
      "narration": "In nineteen oh six, off the coast of Ecuador and Colombia, an earthquake of about magnitude eight point eight caused a tsunami.",
      "on_screen_text": "Ecuador, 1906",
      "highlight_words": [
        "1906"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Ecuador and the Pacific"
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_row",
      "narration": "The whole Pacific coast, from Chile to Alaska and Japan, is lined with these plate collisions.",
      "on_screen_text": "A ring around the Pacific",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Pacific"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_speed",
      "narration": "That's why warning systems exist: buoys and sensors at sea detect the waves and alert the coast.",
      "on_screen_text": "Buoys that warn",
      "highlight_words": [
        "warn"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_speed",
      "narration": "Its speed depends on depth: the deeper the ocean, the faster the wave moves.",
      "on_screen_text": "Deeper means faster",
      "highlight_words": [
        "faster"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_retreat",
      "narration": "The most important part. If you're on the coast and the ground shakes hard or for a long time, don't wait for the alarm.",
      "on_screen_text": "Don't wait for the alarm",
      "highlight_words": [
        "alarm"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "How to stay safe"
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_retreat",
      "narration": "Move away from the sea and get to high ground, or as far inland as you can, on foot if needed.",
      "on_screen_text": "Get to high ground",
      "highlight_words": [
        "high"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_retreat",
      "narration": "And if you see the sea pull back, never go down to look. That's exactly the time to get away.",
      "on_screen_text": "Never go look",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Never"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_retreat",
      "narration": "Learn your area's evacuation routes and the nearest high ground ahead of time. Many beaches have signs showing them.",
      "on_screen_text": "Know your route",
      "highlight_words": [
        "route"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_grow",
      "narration": "Stay on high ground for several hours, until the authorities say it's safe to return.",
      "on_screen_text": "Wait several hours",
      "highlight_words": [
        "hours"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_grow",
      "narration": "Often it doesn't arrive as a breaking wave but as a tide that rises and rises, sweeping everything along.",
      "on_screen_text": "A tide that won't stop",
      "highlight_words": [
        "tide"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_pacific",
      "narration": "Surprise: some tsunamis cross entire oceans and still have strength on the far side of the planet.",
      "on_screen_text": "They cross the planet",
      "highlight_words": [
        "planet"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s29",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_small",
      "narration": "So a tsunami isn't a giant surfing wave: it's the whole ocean moving at once.",
      "on_screen_text": "The whole ocean moves",
      "highlight_words": [
        "whole"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_outro",
      "narration": "Share this video with someone who lives near the sea. Knowing this can save lives.",
      "on_screen_text": "Share it",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Share"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    }
  ],
  "description": "How a tsunami forms, why it travels so fast, why it grows near the coast and how to stay safe. With the cases of Chile 1960 and Ecuador 1906. Original 3D animation; sizes and distances are not to scale.",
